From: Koral Ilgun <koral.ilgun@smartrg.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:18:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: expedite the RCU waits of a station removal

mac80211 waits for RCU readers several times when hostapd removes a
station: once when it deletes a key, once when the station loses its
authorization, once for each TX aggregation session, once between
the two parts of the removal and once when the tailroom count rises.
These waits call synchronize_net(), which is expedited only under
the RTNL. Since a05829a7222e ("cfg80211: avoid holding the RTNL when
calling the driver") a station or key command holds the wiphy mutex
instead, so each wait takes a full grace period, and no other
nl80211 command of the wiphy runs in that time.

hostapd removes the old entry of a station before it answers a new
authentication, or a reassociation after FT over the DS. With HZ=100
the answer comes after the retry time of the station, which sends
its request again. hostapd handles the second request as a new
exchange, and the roam fails. A deauthentication blocks hostapd in
the same way: it deletes the pairwise key and removes the station
while the next frame of that station waits.

Expedite these waits, as synchronize_net() does under the RTNL.
---
 net/mac80211/agg-tx.c      |    2 +-
 net/mac80211/ieee80211_i.h |   10 ++++++++++
 net/mac80211/key.c         |    4 ++--
 net/mac80211/sta_info.c    |    4 ++--
 4 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/net/mac80211/agg-tx.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/agg-tx.c
@@ -397,7 +397,7 @@ int __ieee80211_stop_tx_ba_session(struc
 	 * the aggregation session is no longer OPERATIONAL.
 	 */
 	if (!local->in_reconfig)
-		synchronize_net();
+		ieee80211_synchronize_net_expedited();
 
 	tid_tx->stop_initiator = reason == AGG_STOP_PEER_REQUEST ?
 					WLAN_BACK_RECIPIENT :
--- a/net/mac80211/ieee80211_i.h
+++ b/net/mac80211/ieee80211_i.h
@@ -1981,6 +1981,16 @@ static inline bool ieee80211_sdata_runni
 	return test_bit(SDATA_STATE_RUNNING, &sdata->state);
 }
 
+/*
+ * For a wait under the wiphy mutex, which blocks every nl80211 command of
+ * the wiphy. synchronize_net() is expedited only under the RTNL, and
+ * cfg80211 does not hold the RTNL for a station or a key command.
+ */
+static inline void ieee80211_synchronize_net_expedited(void)
+{
+	synchronize_rcu_expedited();
+}
+
 int ieee80211_hw_config(struct ieee80211_local *local, int radio_idx,
 			u32 changed);
 int ieee80211_hw_conf_chan(struct ieee80211_local *local);
--- a/net/mac80211/key.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/key.c
@@ -102,7 +102,7 @@ static void increment_tailroom_need_coun
 		 * Flush all XMIT packets currently using HW encryption or no
 		 * encryption at all if the count transition is from 0 -> 1.
 		 */
-		synchronize_net();
+		ieee80211_synchronize_net_expedited();
 	}
 }
 
@@ -796,7 +796,7 @@ static void ieee80211_key_destroy(struct
 	 * Synchronize so the TX path and rcu key iterators
 	 * can no longer be using this key before we free/remove it.
 	 */
-	synchronize_net();
+	ieee80211_synchronize_net_expedited();
 
 	__ieee80211_key_destroy(key, delay_tailroom);
 }
--- a/net/mac80211/sta_info.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/sta_info.c
@@ -1520,7 +1520,7 @@ static int _sta_info_move_state(struct s
 			 * on how the hardware offload works.
 			 */
 			if (local->ops->set_key) {
-				synchronize_net();
+				ieee80211_synchronize_net_expedited();
 				if (local->ops->flush_sta)
 					drv_flush_sta(local, sta->sdata, sta);
 				else
@@ -1669,7 +1669,7 @@ int __must_check __sta_info_destroy(stru
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
-	synchronize_net();
+	ieee80211_synchronize_net_expedited();
 
 	__sta_info_destroy_part2(sta, true);
 
